Z||000000||Phil||10-31-2000||08:55 PM||||A fella called me the other day about his 87 V6 auto SE  with a starting problem. I went over to give him a hand but this one has me stumped. His car was running then he washed it, started it and after about 2 mins it sputtered and pumped out black smoke never to start again. One new coil and two rebuilt distributors later the sucker still won't start. Definately has fuel (plugs get wet after cranking) the blasted thing pops and tries a bit before the plugs load up again. A compression check shows all to be fine. The rotor turns and everything to be tight and all. The spark is a little yellow though. Any ideas? Maybe he'll get discusted and let me have it for a song. heheheh||||reg||1
